WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.746
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.046 --> 00:00:08.189
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.489 --> 00:00:14.288
Unit three: Travel Tales. In this unit, you will tell stories about trips and travel problems.

4
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:16.505
delayed flight.

5
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:20.342
delayed flight means a plane that leaves later than planned.

6
00:00:20.642 --> 00:00:22.897
Our delayed flight finally left at midnight.

7
00:00:23.597 --> 00:00:25.855
Your turn. Say: delayed flight.

8
00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:29.777
delayed flight.

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:31.819
missed connection.

10
00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:36.551
missed connection means failing to catch your next plane, train or bus.

11
00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:39.640
Because of the storm, we had a missed connection in Bangkok.

12
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.458
Your turn. Say: missed connection.

13
00:00:45.158 --> 00:00:46.530
missed connection.

14
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:48.378
stranded.

15
00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:51.241
stranded means unable to leave a place.

16
00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:53.935
We were stranded at the airport for ten hours.

17
00:00:54.635 --> 00:00:56.869
Your turn. Say: stranded.

18
00:00:59.569 --> 00:01:00.443
stranded.

19
00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.614
breathtaking view.

20
00:01:03.314 --> 00:01:05.778
breathtaking view means a very beautiful sight.

21
00:01:06.078 --> 00:01:09.006
From the top of Bokor, there's a breathtaking view of the sea.

22
00:01:09.706 --> 00:01:12.126
Your turn. Say: breathtaking view.

23
00:01:14.826 --> 00:01:16.129
breathtaking view.

24
00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:18.106
get lost.

25
00:01:18.806 --> 00:01:21.804
get lost means to not know where you are or how to get somewhere.

26
00:01:22.104 --> 00:01:24.069
We got lost in the old city without a map.

27
00:01:24.769 --> 00:01:27.653
Your turn. Say: get lost.

28
00:01:30.353 --> 00:01:31.308
get lost.

29
00:01:32.317 --> 00:01:33.573
off the beaten track.

30
00:01:34.273 --> 00:01:37.852
off the beaten track means far from the places most tourists visit.

31
00:01:38.152 --> 00:01:40.569
We found a quiet village off the beaten track.

32
00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:43.875
Your turn. Say: off the beaten track.

33
00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:47.924
off the beaten track.

34
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:50.022
unforgettable.

35
00:01:50.722 --> 00:01:54.115
unforgettable means so special that you will always remember it.

36
00:01:54.415 --> 00:01:56.949
Watching the sunrise at Angkor was unforgettable.

37
00:01:57.649 --> 00:01:59.778
Your turn. Say: unforgettable.

38
00:02:02.478 --> 00:02:03.723
unforgettable.

39
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:05.567
hitchhike.

40
00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:10.031
hitchhike means to travel by getting free rides from passing drivers.

41
00:02:10.331 --> 00:02:13.364
In the past, many students hitchhiked across Europe.

42
00:02:14.064 --> 00:02:16.472
Your turn. Say: hitchhike.

43
00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.162
hitchhike.

44
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.045
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:23.345 --> 00:02:26.761
Mr. Daniel, what was your most unforgettable trip?

46
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.515
A trip to Laos. We were travelling by bus when it broke down.

47
00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:35.005
Oh no! Were you stranded?

48
00:02:36.317 --> 00:02:40.827
Yes. We had already missed our connection, so we hitchhiked to the next town.

49
00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:43.838
That sounds scary!

50
00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.264
It was, but we found a breathtaking view off the beaten track.

51
00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:52.037
Grammar focus: Narrative tenses.

52
00:02:52.337 --> 00:02:55.416
To tell a story, use the past simple for the main events.

53
00:02:55.716 --> 00:03:00.421
Use the past continuous for background actions, and the past perfect for earlier events.

54
00:03:00.721 --> 00:03:03.417
For example: When we arrived, the bus had already left.

55
00:03:03.717 --> 00:03:07.458
Use the past perfect to show that one past action happened before another.

56
00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.207
Now read and listen. A Night at the Airport.

57
00:03:11.507 --> 00:03:14.168
Last December, Sophy was flying home from Seoul.

58
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:18.667
While she was waiting at the gate, the screen showed a delayed flight.

59
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:23.701
By the time the plane landed in Bangkok, her connection had already left.

60
00:03:25.017 --> 00:03:28.433
She was stranded for a night, but the airline gave her a free hotel room.

61
00:03:29.717 --> 00:03:32.610
She says it became one of her most unforgettable trips.

62
00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:36.209
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:36.509 --> 00:03:39.368
Far from the places most tourists visit means blank.

64
00:03:39.668 --> 00:03:43.286
A, off the beaten track. B, stranded. C, hitchhike.

65
00:03:47.283 --> 00:03:49.399
The answer is A: off the beaten track.

66
00:03:50.883 --> 00:03:52.651
We blank dinner when the phone rang.

67
00:03:52.951 --> 00:03:56.116
A, had. B, were having. C, have had.

68
00:04:00.117 --> 00:04:01.989
The answer is B: were having.

69
00:04:03.483 --> 00:04:05.692
When I got to the station, the train blank.

70
00:04:05.992 --> 00:04:09.158
A, had left. B, was leaving. C, leaves.

71
00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.219
The answer is A: had left.

72
00:04:16.717 --> 00:04:18.658
A very beautiful sight is a blank.

73
00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.913
A, missed connection. B, breathtaking view. C, delayed flight.

74
00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:29.160
The answer is B: breathtaking view.

75
00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.427
According to the text, Sophy was stranded in blank.

76
00:04:33.727 --> 00:04:36.916
A, Seoul. B, Bangkok. C, Phnom Penh.

77
00:04:40.917 --> 00:04:43.206
The answer is B: Bangkok.

78
00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:48.379
Now it's your turn to speak. Tell me about a trip where something went wrong.

79
00:04:53.679 --> 00:04:59.278
Once, I got lost in Siem Reap, but a friendly tuk-tuk driver helped me find my hotel.

80
00:04:59.578 --> 00:05:01.217
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:02.217 --> 00:05:05.902
Great work today! You learned eight new words and narrative tenses.

82
00:05:06.202 --> 00:05:09.528
Today's value is courage. Try new things and be brave.

83
00:05:09.828 --> 00:05:12.004
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

84
00:05:12.304 --> 00:05:14.875
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

